    {
      "_id": "sqgazyATAbR5wgND",
      "name": "Charm",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/sword.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The dread lord targets one humanoid it can see within 30 feet of itself. If the target can see the dread lord, the target must succeed on a DC 19 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed. The charmed target regards the nathrezim as a trusted friend to be heeded and protected. The target isn't under the dread lord's control, but it takes the dread lord's requests and action in the most favorable way. Each time the dread lord or its companions do anything harmful to the target, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. Otherwise, the effect last 24 hours or until the dread lord is destroyed, is on a different place of existence than the target, or takes a bonus action to end this effect.</p>",
